Author: Alyta Phoenix <alyta@phoenixes.net>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 18:49:36 2026 +0100

    fix(cluster): single image-rejection choke point for text-only VLM deployments
    
    jundot's #2845 review: the fail-closed image rejection only covered
    /v1/chat/completions -- /v1/messages still silently dropped image blocks
    for a text-only distributed VLM deployment (preserve_images keyed on
    is_vlm, which is False for the distributed engine), exactly the outcome
    #1261/#1426 refused. Extracted _reject_image_content_for_text_only_deployment
    as a single pre-extraction choke point and wired it into both routes
    (server.py) so a route added later inherits the same fail-closed behavior.
    
    Also addresses the rest of that review:
    - model_loading.py's narrower _VLM_VISION_PREFIXES is gone; planner.py's
      vision-tensor exclusion now reuses model_discovery's _VISION_WEIGHT_PREFIXES.
    - MTP-tensor exclusion (the language_model.mtp.layers.0 / layer-0 collision)
      is unconditional now, not gated on VLM-ness -- a pure-text -mtp checkpoint
      has the identical collision.
    - inspect_safetensors_layout/complete_model_layout gained a `text_only`
      parameter driven by the caller's own deployment intent (ClusterDeployment
      .text_only / ClusterPlanRequest.text_only), not the checkpoint's shape --
      the catalogue (no text_only passed) keeps advertising full sizes for
      un-flagged VLMs; a concrete text-only deployment sizes against what it
      will actually load. Layout cache key extended to (path, text_only) so the
      two measurements of the same checkpoint don't collide.
    - _supports_pipeline's post-#2819 vision-subconfig guard (which reports no
      pipeline support for any VLM, since mlx-vlm's wrapper doesn't expose it)
      now only applies when text_only=False: a text-only deployment loads
      through plain mlx-lm, the same module a pure-text checkpoint of that
      architecture would use, so the guard's premise doesn't hold there.
    
    Known gap, left for a follow-up rather than rushed under this review's
    scope: remote_model_layout (SSH-probed peer layout) doesn't yet thread
    text_only through to the remote snippet, so a text-only deployment whose
    model_source is a remote peer still sizes full (safe direction -- an
    over-, not under-, estimate). /v1/responses has the same preserve-images-
    keyed-on-is_vlm gap as the two fixed routes but wasn't part of this
    review's named blocker; noted for follow-up, not fixed here.
    
    Rebased cleanly onto main (2 conflicts in engine_pool.py/model_loading.py,
    both from main independently landing overlapping plumbing since this PR
    forked -- resolved by keeping main's already-computed deployment routing
    and dropping the batched-only re-gate it superseded). Full 10,479-test
    suite passes; 5 tests proven to discriminate against the pre-fix code via
    stash-revert.
    
